{% section %}
## Part III. Summary

{% lines %}
- {% line index="16" %}
  - {% instructions %}
    Combine lines 7 and 15 and enter the result

    - If line 16 is a gain, enter the amount from line 16 on Form 1040, 1040-SR, or 1040-NR, line 7a. Then, go to line 17 below.
    - If line 16 is a loss, skip lines 17 through 20 below. Then, go to line 21. Also be sure to complete line 22.
    - If line 16 is zero, skip lines 17 through 21 below and enter -0- on Form 1040, 1040-SR, or 1040-NR, line 7a. Then, go to line 22.
    {% /instructions %}
  - {% box identifier="16" %}
    {% value type="sum" %}
    - {% value type="box_reference" box="7" /%}
    - {% value type="box_reference" box="15" /%}
    {% /value %}
    {% /box %}
  {% /line %}
- {% line index="17" %}
  - {% instructions %}
    Are lines 15 and 16 both gains?

    - Yes. Go to line 18.
    - No. Skip lines 18 through 21, and go to line 22.
    {% /instructions %}
  - {% box identifier="17" %}
    {% value type="conjunction" %}
    - {% value type="comparison" strict=true %}
      - {% value type="box_reference" box="15" /%}
      - {% value slot="minimum" type="number_constant" value=0 /%}
      {% /value %}
    - {% value type="comparison" strict=true %}
      - {% value type="box_reference" box="16" /%}
      - {% value slot="minimum" type="number_constant" value=0 /%}
      {% /value %}
    {% /value %}
    {% /box %}
  {% /line %}
- {% line index="18" %}
  - {% instructions %}If you are required to complete the 28% Rate Gain Worksheet (see instructions), enter the amount, if any, from line 7 of that worksheet{% /instructions %}
  - {% box identifier="18" %}
    {% value type="number_input" %}
    - {% value slot="skipCondition" type="disjunction" %}
      - {% value type="comparison" %}
        - {% value type="box_reference" box="16" /%}
        - {% value slot="maximum" type="number_constant" value=0 /%}
        {% /value %}
      - {% value type="logical_negation" %}
        - {% value type="box_reference" box="17" /%}
        {% /value %}
      {% /value %}
    {% /value %}
    {% /box %}
  {% /line %}
- {% line index="19" %}
  - {% instructions %}If you are required to complete the Unrecaptured Section 1250 Gain Worksheet (see instructions), enter the amount, if any, from line 18 of that worksheet{% /instructions %}
  - {% box identifier="19" %}
    {% value type="number_input" %}
    - {% value slot="skipCondition" type="disjunction" %}
      - {% value type="comparison" %}
        - {% value type="box_reference" box="16" /%}
        - {% value slot="maximum" type="number_constant" value=0 /%}
        {% /value %}
      - {% value type="logical_negation" %}
        - {% value type="box_reference" box="17" /%}
        {% /value %}
      {% /value %}
    {% /value %}
    {% /box %}
  {% /line %}
- {% line index="20" %}
  - {% instructions %}
    Are lines 18 and 19 both zero or blank and you are not filing Form 4952?

    - Yes. Complete the Qualified Dividends and Capital Gain Tax Worksheet in the instructions for Form 1040, line 16. Don't complete lines 21 and 22 below.
    - No. Complete the Schedule D Tax Worksheet in the instructions. Don't complete lines 21 and 22 below.
    {% /instructions %}
  - {% box identifier="20" format="yes_no" %}
    {% value type="conjunction" %}
    - {% value type="logical_negation" %}
      - {% value type="box_reference" box="18" /%}
      {% /value %}
    - {% value type="logical_negation" %}
      - {% value type="box_reference" box="19" /%}
      {% /value %}
    {% /value %}
    {% /box %}
  {% /line %}
- {% line index="21" %}
  - {% instructions %}
    If line 16 is a loss, enter here and on Form 1040, 1040-SR, or 1040-NR, line 7a, the smaller of:

    - The loss on line 16; or
    - ($3,000), or if married filing separately, ($1,500)
    {% /instructions %}
  - {% box identifier="21" %}
    {% value type="conditional" %}
    - {% value slot="condition" type="comparison" strict=true %}
      - {% value type="box_reference" box="16" /%}
      - {% value slot="maximum" type="number_constant" value=0 /%}
      {% /value %}
    - {% value slot="trueValue" type="maximum" %}
      - {% value type="box_reference" box="16" /%}
      - {% value type="filing_status_map" %}
        - {% value
             type="number_constant"
             value=-1500
             filingStatusKey="married_filing_separately" /%}
        - {% value slot="default" type="number_constant" value=-3000 /%}
        {% /value %}
      {% /value %}
    - {% value slot="falseValue" type="number_constant" value=0 /%}
    {% /value %}
    {% /box %}
  {% /line %}
- {% line index="22" %}
  - {% instructions %}
    Do you have qualified dividends on Form 1040, 1040-SR, or 1040-NR, line 3a?

    - Yes. Complete the Qualified Dividends and Capital Gain Tax Worksheet in the instructions for Form 1040, line 16.
    - No. Complete the rest of Form 1040, 1040-SR, or 1040-NR.
    {% /instructions %}
  - {% box identifier="22" format="yes_no" %}
    {% value type="box_reference" box="3a" form="f1040" required=true /%}
    {% /box %}
  {% /line %}
- {% line index="virtual_f1040_7a" virtual=true %}
  - {% instructions %}Value to enter on Form 1040, line 7a{% /instructions %}
  - {% box identifier="virtual_f1040_7a" %}
    {% value type="conditional" %}
    - {% value slot="condition" type="comparison" %}
      - {% value type="box_reference" box="16" /%}
      - {% value slot="minimum" type="number_constant" value=0 /%}
      {% /value %}
    - {% value slot="trueValue" type="box_reference" box="16" /%}
    - {% value slot="falseValue" type="box_reference" box="21" /%}
    {% /value %}
    {% /box %}
  {% /line %}
{% /lines %}
{% /section %}
{% /form %}
